# MySQL Database Configuration for ATOM QMS

## Environment Variables Template

Copy this to your `.env` file and fill in your database credentials:

```env
# ============================================================
# DATABASE CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================

# MySQL Server Connection
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=3306
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=your_secure_password
DB_NAME=railway

# Connection Pool Settings
DB_CONNECTION_LIMIT=10
DB_QUEUE_LIMIT=0
DB_ENABLE_INSECURE_AUTH=false

# Timezone
DB_TIMEZONE=+00:00

# ============================================================
# API SERVER CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================

# Server Port
PORT=5000

# Node Environment
NODE_ENV=development

# ============================================================
# SECURITY CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================

# JWT Secret (for authentication tokens)
JWT_SECRET=your_super_secret_jwt_key_change_this_in_production

# JWT Expiration (in days)
JWT_EXPIRATION=7

# CORS Configuration
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:3000

# ============================================================
# APPLICATION SETTINGS
# ============================================================

# Logging Level (development, info, warn, error)
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Enable Debug Mode
DEBUG=false

# ============================================================
# FILE UPLOAD CONFIGURATION (if using external storage)
# ============================================================

# AWS S3 (optional)
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_aws_access_key
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_aws_secret_key
AWS_S3_BUCKET=atom-qms-images
AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# Or Azure Blob Storage (optional)
AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT=your_storage_account
AZURE_STORAGE_KEY=your_storage_key
AZURE_CONTAINER=exam-images

# ============================================================
# EMAILS (optional - for notifications)
# ============================================================

SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your_email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=your_app_password
SMTP_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@examguard.com

# ============================================================
# BACKUP CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================

# Backup directory path
BACKUP_DIR=/backups/atom-qms

# Enable automatic daily backups
AUTO_BACKUP=true

# Backup schedule (cron format) - 2 AM daily
BACKUP_SCHEDULE=0 2 * * *
```

## Setup Instructions

### 1. Development Environment

```bash
# Create .env file
cp .env.example .env

# Edit .env with your local database credentials
# On Windows
notepad .env

# On macOS/Linux
nano .env
```

### 2. Local MySQL Setup

```bash
# Start MySQL server
# macOS (with Homebrew)
brew services start mysql

# Windows (cmd as Administrator)
net start MySQL80

# Linux (Ubuntu/Debian)
sudo systemctl start mysql

# Create database
mysql -u root -p

# In MySQL console:
CREATE DATABASE atom_qms;
CREATE USER 'exam_user'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'strong_password_here';
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON atom_qms.* TO 'exam_user'@'localhost';
FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
EXIT;

# Load schema
mysql -u exam_user -p atom_qms < database/schema.sql

# (Optional) Load sample data
mysql -u exam_user -p atom_qms < database/seed-data.sql
```

### 3. Production Environment

```bash
# Production database should be on a secure server
# Use strong passwords and follow security best practices

# Example production .env
DB_HOST=db.example.com
DB_PORT=3306
DB_USER=prod_exam_user
DB_PASSWORD=very_strong_password_here
DB_NAME=atom_qms_prod

# Additional production settings
NODE_ENV=production
DEBUG=false
LOG_LEVEL=warn

# Use environment-specific JWT and other secrets
JWT_SECRET=your_production_jwt_secret
```

## Security Best Practices

### 1. Password Management
- Use strong, randomly generated passwords
- Store credentials in environment variables, NEVER in code
- Change default passwords immediately
- Use different passwords for each environment

### 2. Database User Permissions

```sql
-- Create dedicated database user
CREATE USER 'exam_app'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'strong_password';

-- Grant specific permissions (not all)
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON atom_qms.* TO 'exam_app'@'localhost';

-- Or grant specific tables only
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON atom_qms.exams TO 'exam_app'@'localhost';
GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON atom_qms.candidates TO 'exam_app'@'localhost';

-- Apply changes
FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
```

### 3. Network Security

```bash
# Bind MySQL to localhost only (in /etc/mysql/mysql.conf.d/mysqld.cnf)
bind-address = 127.0.0.1

# For remote connections, use SSH tunnel
ssh -L 3306:localhost:3306 user@remote-server

# Or use VPN/firewall rules
```

### 4. Environment Variables Security

```bash
# Never commit .env file
echo ".env" >> .gitignore
echo ".env.*.secret" >> .gitignore

# Use .env.example with placeholder values
cp .env .env.example
sed -i 's/=.*/=/' .env.example  # Remove actual values
git add .env.example
```

### 5. Connection Security

```javascript
// Enable SSL for remote MySQL connections
const pool = mysql.createPool({
  host: process.env.DB_HOST,
  user: process.env.DB_USER,
  password: process.env.DB_PASSWORD,
  database: process.env.DB_NAME,
  ssl: {
    ca: fs.readFileSync('path/to/ca.pem'),
    cert: fs.readFileSync('path/to/client-cert.pem'),
    key: fs.readFileSync('path/to/client-key.pem'),
    rejectUnauthorized: true
  }
});
```

## Troubleshooting

### Connection Issues

```bash
# Test connection from command line
mysql -h localhost -u exam_user -p atom_qms -e "SHOW TABLES;"

# Check MySQL is running
ps aux | grep mysql
# or
systemctl status mysql

# Check port is accessible
netstat -an | grep 3306
# or
ss -an | grep 3306
```

### Environment Variables Not Loading

```javascript
// Add this at the very top of your app
require('dotenv').config({ path: '.env' });

// Verify variables are loaded
console.log('DB_HOST:', process.env.DB_HOST);
```

### Connection Pool Issues

```javascript
// Check connection pool status
pool.on('error', (err) => {
  console.error('Pool error:', err.code, err.fatal);
});

pool.on('warning', (err) => {
  console.warn('Pool warning:', err);
});

// Test pool connection
pool.getConnection().then(conn => {
  console.log('Connection successful');
  conn.release();
}).catch(err => {
  console.error('Connection failed:', err);
});
```

## Database Verification Checklist

- [ ] MySQL server is running
- [ ] Database `atom_qms` exists
- [ ] All tables created (check schema.sql was executed)
- [ ] User permissions are correct
- [ ] Connection test passes
- [ ] Sample data loaded (if using seed-data.sql)
- [ ] Environment variables are set
- [ ] No SSL errors (if using SSL)

## Common Configuration Patterns

### Local Development
```env
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=3306
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=
NODE_ENV=development
DEBUG=true
```

### Docker Compose
```env
DB_HOST=mysql-container
DB_PORT=3306
DB_USER=exam_user
DB_PASSWORD=exam_password
DB_NAME=atom_qms
```

### AWS RDS
```env
DB_HOST=atom-qms.xxxxx.rds.amazonaws.com
DB_PORT=3306
DB_USER=admin
DB_PASSWORD=your_rds_password
DB_NAME=atom_qms
```

### Azure Database for MySQL
```env
DB_HOST=atom-qms-server.mysql.database.azure.com
DB_PORT=3306
DB_USER=exam_user@atom-qms-server
DB_PASSWORD=your_password
DB_NAME=code_exam_guard
```

